    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "liz b.",
        "date": "2025-05-05T19:31:32Z",
        "id": "68198bd151b33b41d330d3ab",
        "label": "Excellent",
        "locale": "en_US",
        "rating": 10,
        "text": "They had everything we needed! Kitchen, bathroom, beach, etc. it was great!!",
        "title": "Lovely home!"
      },
      {
        "author": "C G.",
        "date": "2025-07-09T21:12:29Z",
        "id": "686f3b902b70e9440a26e0f8",
        "label": "Excellent",
        "locale": "en_US",
        "rating": 10,
        "text": "I took my daughter and six of her friends as a graduation gift from her grandparents. They had a BLAST! The home was clean, beautiful, the aesthetics were perfect, and there was room for everyone. The master bedroom was the PERFECT escape when I needed a break. The home had everything we needed, and things we didn't know we would. The neighborhood was quiet, and most locations we wanted to visit were pretty close. We really enjoyed the home and look forward to the opportunity to visit it again! ♥♥♥",
        "title": "Great Stay!"
      },
      {
        "author": "Candace R.",
        "date": "2024-03-12T04:02:02Z",
        "id": "65efd440fec2f67caa56ce19",
        "label": "Excellent",
        "locale": "en_US",
        "rating": 10,
        "text": "The home is centrally located to hop on bikes and get to various restaurants, shops and the beach! For our group to go to the beach together (6 adults and 1 kid) we were able to drive across the street and park in 5 minutes.\n\nThe home had plenty of space for all adults to lounge, sleep and relax. The amenities in the home were also very well appointed, soap, towels, laundry detergent, bikes, beach gear, cooking needs were also covered for us to have breakfast together in the morning.\n\nThe house had a firepit, neat feature for the cooler nights we stayed. Overall I'd definitely come back to rent this house, the neighborhood was quiet and felt like a home away from home.",
        "title": "Easy stay!"
      },
      {
        "author": "James & Christina S.",
        "date": "2024-01-31T05:02:27Z",
        "id": "65b9d4ed4fd82819a2dbcc15",
        "label": "Excellent",
        "locale": "en_US",
        "rating": 10,
        "text": "YOU WILL NOT BE DISAPPOINTED. This is our 3rd visit to the 30A area and this by far is the nicest home we've stayed in. The 3 floors were wonderful if you're a large family. The bunkroom has built in lights and charging ports for EACH BED. My kids LOVED this feature. Each floor has its own bathroom, which was excellent. The mattresses were so comfortable we are looking into replacing ours at home. We used the fire pit and the grill almost every night. The kitchen is a DREAM and everything you could need is there. It was so lovely that we cooked every night! You do have to cross the highway so if you have little people and were planning on not using vehicles or biking keep that in mind. The garage was STOCKED with everything needed for the beach. Ice chests, floats, chairs etc. So, we drove the 2-minute drive to Inlet beach to carry it all. Make sure you soak it all in in the giant garden tub. Convenient to all of 30 A and PCB as well. I could write a page review on this lovely home.",
        "title": "YOU WILL NOT BE DISAPPOINTED"
      }
    ],
    "total": 4
